        "orario": "16:49",
        "timestamp": 1775832599,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Relentless airstrikes on Beirut's residential areas 'remind Lebanese that Israel is enemy as well' Middle East Issued on: 10/04/2026 - 16:49 Nadia Massih is pleased to welcome Dr. Randa Slim, Director of the Conflict Resolution and Track II Dialogues Program at the Middle East Institute and Fellow at the Foreign Policy Institute of the Johns Hopkins University School of Advanced International Studies (SAIS). According to Dr. Slim, Israeli strikes on Lebanon cannot be credibly framed as targeted operations against Hezbollah, but rather indiscriminate violence causing widespread civilian casualties and intensifying regional tensions. She argues that the events represent a critical inflection point within Lebanese public opinion. Pakistan plays major role trying to mediate an end to Iran war 09/04/2026 Middle East Netanyahu fails to address Israel’s failure to achieve war goals in Iran 09/04/2026 Middle East ‘Collective punishment’: At least 182 killed in Israeli strikes on Lebanon 08/04/2026 Middle East 'Pakistani military calling the shots: Has connections with IRCG, very good relationship with Trump' 08/04/2026 Middle East US-Iran truce: ‘Sensitive behind-the-scenes conversations’ paved way for Pakistan-brokered ceasefire 08/04/2026 Middle East Trump administration's claims of victory in Iran 'really quite hollow', analyst says 08/04/2026 Middle East Netanyahu says Israel ready to 'return to battle at any moment' against Iran 08/04/2026 Middle East Iran continues to target Gulf countries despite ceasefire announcement 08/04/2026 Middle East Iran closes Strait of Hormuz again as Israel pounds Lebanon, air defense systems go off in Tehran 08/04/2026 Middle East"
